### Get indication catalog
# Requer role ADMIN ou MANAGER. EMPLOYEE → 403. Sem token → 401.
# O actor é o Bearer; nenhum body leva actorId.
# Collection vazia: Canal, Campanha, Amigo, cada um com origins: [].
GET http://localhost:3003/api/indication-catalog
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create channel origin
# :id da resposta vai para {{originId}} nos requests seguintes.
# Chaves desconhecidas (position, active) são ignoradas.
POST http://localhost:3003/api/indication-origin
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "categoryId": "canal",
  "name": "Facebook"
}

### Create campaign origin
POST http://localhost:3003/api/indication-origin
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "categoryId": "campanha",
  "name": "Verão"
}

### Correct origin name
# :id é o path. Um id no body é ignorado (o path vence no adaptRoute).
PATCH http://localhost:3003/api/indication-origin/{{originId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Instagram Ads"
}

### End origin
# Sem body. O origin permanece no catálogo com active: false.
POST http://localhost:3003/api/indication-origin/{{originId}}/end
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reopen origin
# Sem body. Segundo reopen do mesmo origin → 200, sem novo interval.
POST http://localhost:3003/api/indication-origin/{{originId}}/reopen
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create origin — Amigo (expect 400)
# categoryId "amigo" não guarda origins. Sem write.
# categoryId desconhecido também → 400.
POST http://localhost:3003/api/indication-origin
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "categoryId": "amigo",
  "name": "João"
}

### Create origin — name already reserved (expect 409)
# Segundo create com o mesmo nome na mesma categoria, qualquer case → 409.
# O mesmo nome na outra categoria → 201.
POST http://localhost:3003/api/indication-origin
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "categoryId": "canal",
  "name": "facebook"
}

### Get catalog — unauthenticated (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:3003/api/indication-catalog
